earances last campaign. Gadjovich is expected to see time on the fourth line once he's available.","player":8479981.0,"return":"2026-11-28","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"FLA"},{"date":"2026-11-15","name":"Jake Neighbours","note":"Neighbours missed Sunday's practice after he logged 16:19 of ice time in Saturday's 4-1 loss to Florida. He has chipped in four goals, nine points, 30 shots on net, 14 blocked shots and 61 hits in 20 appearances this campaign. It's unclear if he will be available for Tuesday's matchup against Anaheim.","player":8482089.0,"return":"2026-11-17","src":"ESPN","status":"Day-To-Day","team":"STL"},{"date":"2026-11-15","name":"Philip Broberg","note":"Broberg didn't participate in Sunday's practice after getting injured in Saturday's 4-1 loss to Florida. He has contributed four goals, 13 points, 42 shots on net and 25 blocked shots in 20 appearances this season. If Broberg is unavailable for Tuesday's matchup against Anaheim, Calle Rosen could make his 2026-27 NHL season debut.","player":8481598.0,"return":"2026-11-17","src":"ESPN","status":"Day-To-Day","team":"STL"},{"date":"2026-11-15","name":"Aleksanteri Kaskimaki","note":"Kaskimaki's status wasn't updated after the contest. The 22-year-old should be considered day-to-day pending an update from the Blues. Jonatan Berggren would likely enter the lineup if Kaskimaki can't play Tuesday versus the Ducks.","player":8483463.0,"return":"2026-11-17","src":"ESPN","status":"Day-To-Day","team":"STL"},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"Torey Krug","note":"Krug's move to long-term injured reserve was partially a financial decision, as it allows the Blues to exceed the salary cap by $4 million. The 35-year-old blueliner hasn't played since the 2023-24 campaign, but he hasn't officially ruled out a return. Regardless of when he decides to hang up his skates, the 13-year NHL veteran will be remembered as an excellent two-way player, as he currently sits at 483 points, 621 hits and 832 blocked shots across 778 regular-season outings.","player":8476792.0,"return":"2027-07-01","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"STL"},{"date":"2026-10-10","name":"Dillon Dube","note":"ir","player":8479346.0,"return":"2026-12-04","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"STL"},{"date":"2026-09-30","name":"Tyler Tucker","note":"Based on Tucker's timeline, he shouldn't be expected back until mid-November, though it could certainly be longer. With Logan Mailloux (hand) also sidelined long-term, Adam Jiricek could see an extended run on the blue line. For his part, even once cleared to play, Tucker is unlikely to offer much in the way of fantasy value given his limited offensive upside.","player":8481006.0,"return":"2026-11-17","src":"ESPN","status":"Injured Reserve","team":"STL"},{"date":"2026-10-01","name":"Aleksander Barkov","note":"Lower Body: The Florida Panthers said on Tuesday (Nov. 10) that Barkov is within two weeks of returning to the lineup.","player":8477493.0,"return":null,"src":"HR","status":"Out","team":"FLA"},{"date":"2026-09-29","name":"Jonah Gadjovich","note":"Upper-body: The Florida Panthers placed F Jonah Gadjovich on injured reserve on Tuesday (Sep. 29) and is OUT indefinitely.","player":8479981.0,"return":null,"src":"HR","status":"Out","team":"FLA"},{"date":"2026-10-06","name":"Brad Marchand","note":"Leg: The Florida Panthers said on Tuesday (Nov. 10) that Marchand is within two weeks of returning to the lineup.","player":8473419.0,"return":null,"src":"HR","status":"Out","team":"FLA"},{"date":"2026-11-14","name":"Philip Broberg","note":"Lower Body: Broberg sustained a lower-body injury and won't return to Saturday's (Nov. 14) game versus the Panthers, Alex Ferrario of 101 ESPN reports.","player":8481598.0,"return":null,"src":"HR","status":"Out","team":"STL"},{"date":"2026-10-09","name":"Dillon Dube","note":"Neck: The Blues said on Saturday (Oct. 10) that Dube will be out of action for at least eight weeks and placed on Injured Reserve.","player":8